{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Close attempt (sanctioned non-force path) — STILL OPEN, as expected.\n\n1) 'rebar transition 3b92-8ef3-661b-49b2 open closed' failed with:\n   plan-review close gate: unsigned: no certified plan-review attestation. Run rebar review-plan 3b92-8ef3-661b-49b2 separately, then retry close.\n\n2) Ran the legitimate remedy 'rebar review-plan 3b92-8ef3-661b-49b2' (no --force). Verdict: BLOCK (exit 1), 3 blocking findings, signature {signed: false, reason: BLOCK}. The gate independently reached the same conclusion as my triage comment above:\n   - E4: 'the named consumer enumerate_open_count_skew_anomalies and the direct JIRA_*/os.environ + AcliClient construction it claims exist in src/rebar/_engine_support/bridge_fsck.py (~lines 279-291) are absent'.\n   - G1G2: 'the plan's core edit target does not exist in bridge_fsck.py (or anywhere in src/rebar), and bridge_fsck.py contains no AcliClient construction, no JIRA_URL/USER/PROJECT/API_TOKEN reads, and no os.environ access'.\n   - G6: 'the plan's core mechanism targets code that does not exist ... There is nothing to reroute'.\n\nSo both the human read and the gate agree the ACs are unsatisfiable as written. This needs an obsolete-disposition decision from an operator (see the preceding comment for the two options). No --force / --force-close was used."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786087858461032001,"uuid":"5efa7777-43e5-4d76-8465-b436dc6c29eb"}